[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2506873335","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99336#issuecomment-2506873335","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99336","id":2506873335,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Va9n3","user":{"login":"OffsetMOSFET","id":91294328,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMjk0MzI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91294328?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET","html_url":"https://github.com/OffsetMOSFET","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-29T00:14:31Z","updated_at":"2024-11-29T00:14:31Z","body":"Currently, the \"as\" keyword is consistent with using the constructor, which copies.\n\n[https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_packedbytearray.html#class-packedbytearray-constructor-packedbytearray](url)\n\nAlso, I'm confused with your expectation. Shouldn't all the arrays be the same if all reference the same data?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2506873335/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2506888910","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99336#issuecomment-2506888910","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99336","id":2506888910,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VbBbO","user":{"login":"Shadetheartist","id":8973930,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5NzM5MzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8973930?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadetheartist","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadetheartist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadetheartist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadetheartist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadetheartist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadetheartist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadetheartist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadetheartist/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadetheartist/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadetheartist/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadetheartist/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-29T00:36:51Z","updated_at":"2024-11-29T00:36:51Z","body":"Sorry you're right about my expectation being wrong, i didn't double check it. It should be:\n\n```\n[32, 64, 128, 0]\n[32, 64, 128, 0]\n[32, 64, 128, 0]\n```\n\nMy point remains though that the 'as' operator should either have some note on the documentation about this behavior specifically, or otherwise just not copy the data in this unexpected way. The documentation approach is probably the way to go. Even just a note on the `PackedByteArray` page.\n\nThe reason this needs some note is because many programmers are already familiar with how type casting works in C-like languages. In particular, 'Reinterpret Casts' and 'Object Casting', which just tell the compiler to treat the data in a particular way. They do not copy or otherwise mutate the data. \n\nIn C++, for instance\n```\nint funny_number = 69420;\nchar* not_copied = reinterpret_cast<char*>(&value);\n```\n\nor in C\n```\nint funny_number = 69420;\nchar* not_copied = (char*)(&value);\n```\n\nThis is the sort of behavior i have implicitly come to expect from non-primitive mutable data types in most languages. The documentation for `PackedByteArray` saying \"Packed arrays are always passed by reference.\" enforces that idea as well, so it is surprising to me that using the `as` operator, which is akin to type casting, does actually copy the data in this case.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2506888910/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2506927344","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99336#issuecomment-2506927344","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99336","id":2506927344,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VbKzw","user":{"login":"OffsetMOSFET","id":91294328,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMjk0MzI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91294328?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET","html_url":"https://github.com/OffsetMOSFET","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OffsetMOSFET/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-29T01:38:58Z","updated_at":"2024-11-29T01:38:58Z","body":"Well, it's consistent with how static_cast will work on these packed-arrays in C++,  which will use the internal constructor and also mark it for copy-on-write.\n\nI do agree the documentation can be clearer.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2506927344/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2937259076","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99336#issuecomment-2937259076","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99336","id":2937259076,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vEwRE","user":{"login":"ExplodingImplosion","id":60752903,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNzUyOTAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60752903?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ExplodingImplosion","html_url":"https://github.com/ExplodingImplosion","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ExplodingImplosion/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ExplodingImplosion/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ExplodingImplosion/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ExplodingImplosion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ExplodingImplosion/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ExplodingImplosion/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ExplodingImplosion/repos","events_url":"https: